.TH HARBORCTL 8 "July 2026" "Admiral" "Admiral Administration"
.SH NAME
harborctl \- administer the Admiral customer portal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B harborctl
.I COMMAND
\fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B harborctl
provides local administrative commands for the Admiral Harbor customer portal.
It uses the Harbor application configuration and database; it does not bypass
Harbor's application models.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ping
Check connectivity from Harbor to the Admiral control plane.
.TP
.B user create [--type admin|customer] [--display-name NAME] [--country CODE] IDENT
Create an administrator or customer account. The password is read from
.B ADMIRAL_HARBOR_SET_PASSWORD
when set, otherwise it is requested interactively.
.TP
.B user list [--output table|json]
List administrator and customer accounts.
.TP
.B user set-password USERNAME
Set an administrator password.
.TP
.B user toggle-active USERNAME
Toggle an administrator account between active and inactive.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ADMIRAL_HARBOR_SET_PASSWORD
Password used by account creation and password changes. Avoid exposing this
variable in persistent process or shell configuration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/admiral/harbor.env
Packaged Harbor environment configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR admiral-harbor.service (8)
.SH AUTHORS
Admiral Project
